# port-patches.sh: glm/nucleus-race @ 3155e0ea134a over glm/zig-engine-fixes-on-186 @ e027c49cd06d (commits f4bdb3247840..7ffb37f42b63); regenerate with scripts/port-patches.sh, do not edit
glm_cuda: spill v2 for prompts with pictures: points with pictures before their cut written as format v3 on every rank, found only for the same pictures in the same places, with KV sharding too (port of the DeepSeek port's spill-pictures)

The GLM tier kept every point as text (pointKey(keyed, block, no media))
and its keep and lookup dropped the prompt cache's pictures. core/spill's
store side was ready (format v3, pictureId, mediaIds, recovery checks);
this is the tier's half.

- Leader.keep: a write whose key holds pictures records those starting
  before the cut (pointPictures: the keyed ids derive from each digest, the
  model ids hold the placeholder at every picture row and equal the keyed
  ids elsewhere; at most 256), its key adds them (format.pointKey with
  media) and the store keeps the model ids beside the keyed ones; any
  disagreement, more pictures, or TF_GLM_IMAGE_CACHE=0 writes nothing
  (pictures_refused). A cut before every picture is a text point, unchanged.
- Leader.lookupMedia (Tier.lookup with Want.images/media): every picture of
  the key named by its full identity (keyedMedia = prompt_cache.mediaKeys
  over the store's media) or a miss; the store then matches each point's
  pictures before its cut by span and digest, so a changed picture at the
  same rows, the same seed bytes of another digest and a straddling picture
  of another length all miss, a picture past the cut does not matter.
- The keep note: a new op keep_pictures (a keep's fields, then the
  pictures and the placeholder, bounded: 1..256, in order, not overlapping,
  starting before the cut, the placeholder a model id); a text keep is
  `keep`, byte for byte. Rank 1 rebuilds rank 0's keyed and raw ids from its
  own model ids and the noted pictures (followerIds) and writes only when
  the point key is rank 0's: a follower whose picture sits elsewhere writes
  nothing, and rank 0's restore then finds it on no rank and both forget it.
- Counters pictures_kept and pictures_refused (each rank's own, appended to
  TierCounts and the stats ask; /metrics names them).
- Settings.image_cache (TF_GLM_IMAGE_CACHE, both ranks); the fingerprint's
  features carry "image_cache=0;" only when it is off, so the default
  namespace is the one before. The wire version stays 1 (a new op, text
  bytes unchanged). core/spill's format.Media is the prompt cache's Media
  byte for byte (checked at comptime).
- KV sharding (the kv-shard patches): no code change; the lineage's part salt, the home
  part, carries and borrowing are the text paths', and tests pin them for
  pictures.

Switches: none new (TF_GLM_IMAGE_CACHE from the patch before). Text points,
their keys and their bytes are unchanged.

Tests (host): pointPictures and followerIds; a picture point written on both
ranks, restored from disk byte for byte and resumed exactly, also after a
restart, while two different same-size pictures at the same rows and a
forged equal-seed digest miss; a picture straddling the cut (another length
misses), pictures before / straddling / after the cut, a later turn with one
more; a follower whose picture is elsewhere; the image cache off; the
keep_pictures round trip, its refusals and 257 pictures; the features
string. KV sharding: picture keeps salted with their home part and restored
into it, a picture state carried into the other part, a picture prompt
borrowing rows with its pictures attached once and in every segment, SH-1's
refusal order with a real NoVisionTower (reserveMedia before newSeq).

Measured on the pair: not run yet (a picture point restored from disk and
after a restart equal to a cold prefill, with and without KV sharding).

Credits: Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo); spill v2's block
store design (2,048-token blocks, lineage, the write-at-keep ring, release
and fsync order): BadAd84 (https://github.com/BadAd84),
MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold#118; the DeepSeek Zig
port's spill-pictures.
Apply from the checkout root with: git apply 0028-zig-glm-spill-pictures.patch

